Summary for chunk 3:
The official Madrid Guide provides helpful hints, tips, and essential stops for making an unforgettable trip to Madrid. The guide includes information about the city's art scene, including the works of Goya and Velázquez, as well as practical advice for planning a trip. The guide also offers QR codes that can be used to check exhibition schedules, buy tickets online, and get additional information about the city.

The official Madrid Guide is available in various formats, including a PDF guide and mobile apps. It includes information on how long to stay in Madrid, with options ranging from 24 hours to a week. The guide also features panoramic views of the city, an observation deck 92 meters above the ground, and an official shop selling artisan souvenirs.

The guide is produced by MADRID DESTINO CULTURA TURISMO Y NEGOCIO, S.A., and is available in Spanish. It can be downloaded for free from esmadrid.com.
